Papule: Raised, circumscribed, solid lesion (Option A ruled out) &lt; 1cm

{{caption_text}}

Plaque: Elevated circumscribed lesion

(Option B ruled out) &gt; 1cm

{{caption_text}}

Vesicle: Circumscribed elevation less than &lt; 1cm in diameter that contains fluid (clear, serous or haemorrhagic) and is often grouped

{{caption_text}}

Bullae: Bullae are more than &gt; 1cm in diameter (Option D ruled out).

{{caption_text}}

Petechiae: Punctate haemorrhagic spot, approximately 1–2 mm in diameter.

{{caption_text}}

Ecchymoses: A macular area of haemorrhage more than 1cm (bruise) in diameter.

{{caption_text}}

Purpura: Haemorrhagic spots more than 3mm but less than 1cm caused by bleeding underneath the skin

